@startuml UC-MG07-activity
' UC-MG07 Generate and archive periodic reports, as built at the end of Sprint 2.
' Source: use case specification v3.0, narrowed where the team decided otherwise:
' no PDF export, no LLM summary (every report is from the structured template),
' no push to the family, and the family's own reading of reports belongs to UC-FM04.
' Render: java -jar plantuml.jar -tpng UC-MG07-activity.puml
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #444444
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  DiamondBorderColor #444444
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #F8F8F6
  BorderColor #9A9A9A
}
skinparam swimlane {
  BorderColor #888888
  TitleFontStyle bold
}
title UC-MG07  Generate and archive periodic reports\n(one set of facts, three readers)

|Manager|
start
if (What starts the run?) then (the manager)
  :Choose a period on the Reports screen,
  for one elder or for every elder,
  and press Generate;
  |System|
else (the weekly schedule)
  |System|
  :Sunday 23:00, Singapore time:
  last week, every elder with visits in it;
endif

|System|
repeat :Take the next elder;
  :Gather the period's facts once:
  visits and their evidence, vital signs,
  the caregivers' notes, incidents
  with their timelines;
  repeat :Take the next reader (family, regulator, internal);
    if (A report for this elder, period
and reader already on file?) then (yes)
      :Keep the one on file;
      note right
        Running the same period twice,
        by hand or by the schedule,
        files nothing twice.
      end note
    else (no)
      if (Any visit in the period not closed?) then (yes)
        :Mark the data incomplete
        and list each missing visit;
      else (no)
      endif
      :Write the four sections in a fixed order:
      Service completion, Vital signs,
      Observations, Incidents;
      note right
        **Template Method**: the order is final
        and the same for every reader. A reader
        decides only how much of each step it sees:
        caregivers by name or by number,
        vital signs as ranges or every reading,
        notes quoted or only counted, incidents
        with or without who did what.
      end note
      :Add the medical disclaimer
      (family version only);
      :File the report as published;
    endif
  repeat while (Another reader?) is (yes) not (no)
repeat while (Another elder?) is (yes) not (no)

|Manager|
:Open a report from the list:
its sections, completeness,
disclaimer and corrections;
if (Something to correct?) then (yes)
  :Write a correction;
  |System|
  :Append the correction with its author and time,
  the report itself stays as filed;
  note right
    A filed report is never edited or
    deleted: there is no endpoint for
    either, and the report has no setter.
  end note
else (no)
endif
stop
@enduml
